/*
 * No Capacitor plugins run in the Electron main process.
 *
 * Generated by `cap sync`, and deliberately left empty afterwards. The only
 * plugin this app has for Electron is the SQLite one, whose desktop
 * implementation pulls in better-sqlite3-multiple-ciphers -- a native module
 * needing node-gyp and a rebuild against Electron's own ABI, for a catalogue
 * cache the desktop does not keep. See MemoryCatalogueStore: on the desktop the
 * catalogue is held for the session and fetched again next time, which costs
 * one request per category visited and no native compilation at all.
 *
 * Regenerating this file with `cap sync` will put the plugin back. If that
 * happens and the app stops starting with MODULE_NOT_FOUND, this is why.
 */

